_2>=3)=0.\nk=1: 1/4+1/4=1/2. k=2: 1/4+0=1/4. Sum=3/4. \n\nBut E[M_2]=1. Discrepancy! Let me recheck.\n\nHmm, that's wrong. Let me recompute E[M_2]. Paths of length 2:\n++: S_0=0,S_1=1,S_2=2, M=2\n+-: S_0=0,S_1=1,S_2=0, M=1\n-+: S_0=0,S_1=-1,S_2=0, M=0\n--: S_0=0,S_1=-1,S_2=-2, M=0\n\nSo M values: 2,1,0,0. E[M_2] = 3/4. \n\nI made an error above; -+ gives M=0 not 1. So E[M_2]=3/4. Formula gives 3/4. ✓ \n\nSo my formula and computation are correct. E[M_11] = 565/256.\n\nLet me re-verify the sum once more carefully.\n\nP(S_11 >= k):\n- k=1: sum of P(S=1,3,5,7,9,11) = 462+330+165+55+11+1 = 1024. /2048\n- k=2: P(S=3,5,7,9,11) = 330+165+55+11+1 = 562. /2048\n- k=3: same = 562\n- k=4: P(S=5,7,9,11) = 165+55+11+1 = 232\n- k=5: 232\n- k=6: P(S=7,9,11) = 55+11+1 = 67\n- k=7: 67\n- k=8: P(S=9,11) = 11+1 = 12\n- k=9: 12\n- k=10: P(S=11) = 1\n- k=11: 1\n\nP(S_11 >= k+1) = P(S_11 >= 2), P(S_11>=3), ..., P(S_11>=12):\nP(S>=2)=562, P(S>=3)=562, P(S>=4)=232, P(S>=5)=232, P(S>=6)=67, P(S>=7)=67, P(S>=8)=12, P(S>=9)=12, P(S>=10)=1, P(S>=11)=1, P(S>=12)=0.\n\nP(M>=k) = P(S>=k)+P(S>=k+1):\nk=1: 1024+562 = 1586\nk=2: 562+562 = 1124\nk=3: 562+232 = 794\nk=4: 232+232 = 464\nk=5: 232+67 = 299\nk=6: 67+67 = 134\nk=7: 67+12 = 79\nk=8: 12+12 = 24\nk=9: 12+1 = 13\nk=10: 1+1 = 2\nk=11: 1+0 = 1\n\nSum = 1586+1124+794+464+299+134+79+24+13+2+1\n1586+1124=2710\n2710+794=3504\n3504+464=3968\n3968+299=4267\n4267+134=4401\n4401+79=4480\n4480+24=4504\n4504+13=4517\n4517+2=4519\n4519+1=4520\n\n4520/2048 = 565/256.\n\nSo the expected value is 565/256.", "tool_calls": [], "created_at": 1786709882}
